 ## Tensor Fields and Dimensional Collapse
 
 The full Kundli phase space is computationally intractable: nine grahas × twelve houses × twenty-seven Nakshatras × sixteen Vargas × continuous longitudinal positions. The system solves this through two compression operations.
 
-Ashtakavarga projects the 9-dimensional graha space onto a 2-dimensional binary grid: 8 grahas × 12 houses = 96 bindu/no-bindu cells. This is principal component analysis performed by hand, centuries before Pearson formalized the mathematics. The Jyotishi does not read the hypercube. The Jyotishi reads the shadow it casts on chart paper.
